cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these research materials, please cite them as below, and also
  cite the two dataset papers listed under references.
title: "Wearable Infection Detection: Sampling Schedules Under Modelled Energy Budgets"
abstract: >-
  Research materials and results of a retrospective study that compared sparse
  wearable heart-rate sampling schedules, held to the same modelled energy
  budget, on two public COVID-19 wearable datasets. The primary analysis did
  not support an advantage for fixed-clock nighttime sampling over evenly
  spaced sampling. The repository contains the protocol and amendments, the
  analysis code and tests, aggregate results, documented limitations and the
  verification carried out for publication.
